ADDENDA <Act No. 11457, Jun. 1, 2012>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force one year after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (General transitional measures concerning disposition)
Dispositions issued, procedures taken, or acts done by or against administrative agencies under the previous Seed Industry Act before this Act enters into force shall be deemed corresponding dispositions, procedures, acts done or against administrative agencies under this Act.
Article 3 (Transitional measures concerning registration of plant variety managers, reporting on representative of multiple parties)
(1) A person who has registered the appointment and change of a plant variety manager and the grant or revocation of agency authority under Article 3(3) of the previous Seed Industry Act as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed to have registered the appointment and change of a plant variety manager and the grant or revocation of agency authority under Article 4(3).
(2) A representative of multiple parties reported under the proviso of Article 5(1) of the previous Seed Industry Act as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed a representative of multiple parties reported under the proviso of Article 7(1).
(3) A person who has reported succession to a right to plant variety protection under Article 23 of the previous Seed Industry Act as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed to have reported a right to plant variety protection under Article 27.
Article 3-2 (Transitional measures concerning protection of known plant varieties)
Where an application for plant variety protection is filed or plant variety protection is granted after an application for plant variety protection was filed pursuant to Article 13-2 of the previous Seed Industry Act as at the time this Act enters into force, Article 13-2 of the previous Seed Industry Act shall apply to the plant variety right.
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning applications, requests for plant variety protection and registration thereof)
(1) A person who files an application for plant variety protection under Article 26 of the previous Seed Industry Act as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed to have filed an application for plant variety protection under Article 30.
(2) The establishment, etc. of a plant variety right, exclusive license or non-exclusive license registered under Article 68 of the previous Seed Industry Act as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed registered under Article 52.
(3) A person who has filed a request for adjudication on the establishment of a non-exclusive license under Article 68 of the previous Seed Industry Act as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed to have filed a request for adjudication under Article 67.
Article 5 (Transitional measures concerning establishment of Variety Protection Adjudication Committee)
(1) The Variety Protection Adjudication Committee established under Article 91(1) of the previous Seed Industry Act as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed the Tribunal established under Article 90(1).
(2) The adjudication members of the Variety Protection Adjudication Committee appointed or commissioned under Article 91(2) of the previous Seed Industry Act as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed the adjudicators appointed or entrusted under Article 90(2). In such cases, the term of office of a commissioned adjudicator shall be the remaining term of office of his or her predecessor.
Article 6 (Transitional measures concerning requests for adjudication)
(1) A person who has filed a request for trial on decision of rejection or decision of revocation or trial for invalidation under Article 93 or 94 of the previous Seed Industry Act as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed to have filed a request for adjudication on decision of rejection or decision of revocation or adjudication on invalidation under Article 91 or 92.
(2) A person who has filed a request for retrial or an objection to a trial decision by deception under Article 101 or 102 of the previous Seed Industry Act as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed to have filed a request for retrial or an objection to a trial decision by deception under Article 99 or 100.
Article 7 (Transitional measures concerning applications for registration of denominations of plant varieties)
(1) A person who has filed an application to register a denomination of a plant variety under Article 111(1) of the previous Seed Industry Act as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed to have filed an application to register the denomination of a plant variety under Article 109(1).
(2) The denomination of a plant variety registered under Article 111(8) of the previous Seed Industry Act shall be deemed registered under Article 109(8).
(3) A person who has filed an objection to registration of the denomination of a plant variety under Article 111-2 of the previous Seed Industry Act as at the time this Act shall be deemed to have filed an objection to registration of the denomination of a plant variety under Article 110.
Article 8 (Transitional measures concerning establishment of Seed Commission)
(1) The Seed Council established under Article 158(1) of the previous Seed Industry Act as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed the Seed Commission established under Article 118(1).
(2) The Seed Council members appointed or commissioned under Article 158(3) of the previous Seed Industry Act as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed the Seed Commission members appointed or commissioned under Article 118(3). In such cases, the term of office of a commissioned member shall be the remaining term of office of his or her predecessor.
Article 9 (Transitional measures concerning exemption from, or refund or, fees)
An application for exemption from fees or a request for refund of fees filed under Article 161 or 162 of the previous Seed Industry Act as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed an application for exemption or request for refund filed under Article 126.
Article 10 (Transitional measures concerning penalty provisions and administrative fines)
The application of penalty provisions and the imposition of administrative fines for violations committed before this Act enters into force shall be governed by the previous Seed Industry Act.
Article 11 (Relationship to other statutes)
A citation of the previous Seed Industry Act or the provisions thereof in other statutes or regulations as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed a citation of this Act or the provision thereof in lieu of the previous provisions, if corresponding provisions exit herein.

